WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.721
The longest-living goldfish

00:00:01.721 --> 00:00:05.520
on record was 43 years old.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.570
But chances are your goldfish

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.190
didn't even live a quarter that long.

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.650
In fact, most goldfish don't survive

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:16.870
past their fifth birthday,
and that's a major problem

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.799
since they're supposed to live for

00:00:18.799 --> 00:00:20.766
about as long as your cat.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.653
So why are goldfish dying so young?

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:34.810
The usual culprit behind your
goldfish's untimely demise

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:37.200
is, well, poop.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.680
You see, goldfish waste
contains toxins like ammonia

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.420
that can burn gills and
even damage the brain.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.440
In the wild, this isn't a problem.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.390
Freshwater lakes and
ponds are home to armies

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.350
of bacteria that break it down

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:57.230
into less harmful chemicals.
But in your home tank,

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.760
there's no bacteria to be found.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.280
You have to introduce it,
and that's where a lot

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:06.220
of goldfish owners slip
up because you can't

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:09.560
just buy a fish the same
day you get your tank.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:13.179
The process of growing
bacteria takes patience.

00:01:13.179 --> 00:01:15.530
First, you'll need to remove chlorine

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:18.440
from your tank water using a conditioner.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:21.220
Chlorinated tap water
is fine for you to drink

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:24.830
since it kills off germs,
but it's not so great

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:27.510
for the bacteria you want to cultivate.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:31.180
Once you've created a safe
space for the bacteria to grow,

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:34.350
they'll come from all over: the air,

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:36.780
the outside of the tank, and any rocks

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.590
or plants you stick in
the tank for decoration.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:42.680
You can also buy commercially
sold bacteria cultures

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:47.250
grown in labs. After that,
all they need is dinner.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:48.860
Fish food will do.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:51.690
As the food breaks down,
it releases ammonia

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:56.690
for the bacteria to eat, and
finally, you wait for a while.

00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:00.230
Depending on how much
bacteria you start with,

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:02.790
the process can take about two months.

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:06.040
That's right, two months.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:08.640
But then there should be enough bacteria.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.020
You can double-check with
a simple water test kit.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:15.430
But here's the thing, all
the bacteria in the world

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:19.340
won't keep your fish alive
if the tank is too small.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:23.510
You see, as these bacteria
gobble up goldfish poop,

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.910
they produce some waste of their own,

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:28.200
and if it's not sufficiently diluted,

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.660
it can kill your goldfish.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:34.810
A dinky, single-gallon
bowl is much too small,

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:36.965
and even the 10-gallon tank you see

00:02:36.965 --> 00:02:39.580
in every pet store won't cut it.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:42.530
A single adult goldfish
needs at least twice

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:44.255
that much water to thrive.

00:02:44.804 --> 00:02:47.496
That's almost 40 kilograms of water,

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.920
2000 times heavier than your goldfish,

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:53.820
and even with a huge
tank, you'll still need

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:58.000
to replace about 30% of
the water every two weeks

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.370
because besides poop,
goldfish release hormones

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:03.640
and pheromones into their environment,

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:07.090
which, if left unchecked,
can stunt their growth.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.190
That might help explain why goldfish

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:11.815
in healthy environments can reach the size

00:03:11.815 --> 00:03:15.870
of an American football,
while your last goldfish

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.243
wasn't much bigger than your index finger.

00:03:19.081 --> 00:03:21.870
Once you have a big, detoxified tank,

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:26.220
Goldie just needs one more
thing: your attention.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.770
Because you're not swimming
in the tank with her,

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:31.887
it's hard to notice if
something's wrong with, say,

00:03:31.887 --> 00:03:35.850
the water quality. So
oftentimes new goldfish owners

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:39.540
don't realize anything's
amiss until it's too late,

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:43.480
and common diseases like
fin rot, white spot disease,

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:47.080
and fungal infections
have already taken hold.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.960
So it's a good idea to
pay careful attention

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:52.590
to how the water looks and smells,

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:55.030
and anyway, spending time
with your goldfish will

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:57.520
be worth it since you can teach Goldie

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:00.563
to swim through hoops
and eat from your hand.

